      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "The cardiac glycoside SC-4453 had the lowest tissue concentration in brain at steady state in guinea pigs, demonstrating that glycoside-type compounds are generally restricted by the blood-brain barrier.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "Loganin, a glycoside, showed the lowest brain levels after systemic administration in rats, consistent with poor blood-brain barrier penetration for polar glycosides.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "The query is doxorubicin, a P-glycoprotein substrate with known poor baseline brain penetration. Although cyclosporine co-treatment can inhibit efflux, the available transferable evidence from analogous glycosides and P-gp substrates indicates that meaningful CNS access is not established; therefore the prediction is fail.",
